{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1082", "sample_idx": 11, "model_name": "google/gemma-3n-e2b-it", "content": "Arthur awoke to the smell of pine needles and damp earth. Sunlight dappled through the leaves of impossibly tall trees, painting shifting patterns on the forest floor. He sat up, a wave of disorientation washing over him. He wasn't in his apartment. This wasn't his bedroom. He reached out, his hand passing through what felt like solid bark. Panic flared. He looked down and saw his clothes – worn jeans and a faded t-shirt – but they felt…wrong. Too perfect, somehow. He glanced at his hands, noticing the subtle details, the way the light caught the veins beneath his skin. It was all too real, yet…crisp. Like a meticulously rendered digital creation. A small, intricately carved wooden bird landed on his shoulder, chirping a melody that seemed to resonate not just in his ears, but in his very bones.\n\n***\n\nHe stumbled to his feet, heart hammering against his ribs. A shimmering, almost invisible line appeared in the air before him, a faint outline of a path winding through the trees. He instinctively knew he had to follow it. The world around him felt…coded. He noticed the way the leaves rustled with a predictable rhythm, the placement of the rocks, the almost unnervingly vibrant colors. A digital shimmer clung to the edges of everything, a subtle glitch in the fabric of reality. He could *feel* the game mechanics at play, the invisible rules governing his existence. He was a character in a world he didn't understand, a player trapped within the code. He took a shaky breath, the scent of pine now laced with the faint, metallic tang of electricity. The path beckoned, promising adventure, danger, and a terrifying unknown.\n\n\n\n", "logprobs": [{"token": "Arthur", "logprob": -0.7662928104400635}, {"token": "▁awoke", "logprob": -0.4878727197647095}, {"token": "▁to", "logprob": -0.0028092702850699425}, {"token": "▁the", "logprob": -0.00702104065567255}, {"token